"tabBatteries": "Battery maintenance",
"bm_title": "Battery maintenance",
"bm_help": "Change what a Pylontech battery keeps (its clock, its counters, its limits, its outputs, its serial number, even its firmware) through the console of the gateway node it is plugged into, as the maker's own tool does. Each operation is a guided, checked step, never a free command; before and after it the battery is read, and everything is written to the history.",
"bm_admin_only": "Only an administrator can use this screen.",
"bm_off": "Writing to batteries is turned off in the server (it needs ARMOR_BATTERY_WRITE=1), so nothing here can be sent. Turn it on only when you want to work on a battery, and also on the node (Network page of its panel) and in the broker's access list.",
"bm_warning": "What is written goes into the battery's own memory. Some changes cannot be undone, and the maker may refuse the warranty. Nothing here has been tried on a real battery yet: practise each step on a spare one, starting with the clock.",
