"bm_ref_no_answer": "The node did not answer in time.",
"bm_ref_login_failed": "The battery did not accept the service password saved in the node.",
"bm_ref_preflight_failed": "The node could not read the battery before the operation.",
"bm_ref_stage": "The node refused a piece of the firmware file.",
"bm_op_set_clock": "Set the clock",
"bm_opd_set_clock": "Sets the battery's clock to the node's time. Harmless; the first one to try on a spare battery, because it also shows whether the console accepts the way ARMOR writes.",
"bm_op_clear_stats": "Clear the statistics counters",
"bm_opd_clear_stats": "Sets the protection and cycle counters to zero. The old values are lost, so they are kept in the record of this operation first.",
"bm_op_clear_log": "Clear the log",
"bm_opd_clear_log": "Erases the battery's log. It cannot be recovered.",
"bm_op_clear_data": "Clear the event or history records",
"bm_opd_clear_data": "Erases the recorded events or the recorded history of the battery: the evidence of what happened to it. Save it first (the Batteries screen can show it).",
"bm_op_restart": "Restart the battery's system",
"bm_opd_restart": "Restarts the battery's controller. The outputs may blink for a moment. Allowed even with an alarm active.",
"bm_op_shutdown": "Shut the battery down",
"bm_opd_shutdown": "Switches the battery off: the node stops hearing it until someone wakes it up on site (its switch or the wake-up contact). Allowed even with an alarm active.",
"bm_op_soc_capacity": "Write the total capacity",
"bm_opd_soc_capacity": "Writes the maker's capacity for the model (US2000C 50 Ah, US3000C 74 Ah, UP5000 100 Ah) and reads it back. It changes how the battery computes its charge level; the battery must be at rest.",
"bm_op_mosfail_test": "Switch the MOSFET-failure test on",
"bm_opd_mosfail_test": "The 'Set Mosfail test' step of the maker's procedure for a replaced board. Use it only as part of that procedure.",
"bm_op_soc_reset": "Reset the charge level (SOC)",
"bm_opd_soc_reset": "The maker's reset: erases the external memory, restarts the battery, writes the capacity again and writes the serial number back. Everything the battery had learned is lost. Never cut halfway.",
"bm_op_pcb_setup": "Set up a replaced board",
"bm_opd_pcb_setup": "The maker's steps after a board replacement: write the capacity, switch the MOSFET-failure test on, set the clock and write the serial number from the label. Only use it after really replacing the board.",
"bm_op_limits_set": "Change the limits",
"bm_opd_limits_set": "Writes a whole group of thresholds (module voltages, cell voltages or temperatures) and saves them. Wrong values can make the battery stop protecting itself.",
"bm_op_limits_default": "Put the limits back to factory values",
"bm_opd_limits_default": "Restores every threshold to the maker's default and saves. Your own values are lost (they stay in the record of this operation).",
"bm_op_protections_set": "Enable or disable protections",
"bm_opd_protections_set": "Switches individual protections on or off. Disabling one asks you to accept the risk: the battery can be damaged or catch fire.",
"bm_op_protections_default": "Put the protections back to factory settings",
"bm_opd_protections_default": "Restores every protection to the maker's default.",
"bm_op_output_set": "Switch an output",
"bm_opd_output_set": "Switches the charge MOSFET, the discharge MOSFET, the buzzer or the heater, and reads the state back. Switching a MOSFET off cuts the power through the battery. It can be put back as it was.",
"bm_op_fault_clear": "Clear the fuse fault",
"bm_opd_fault_clear": "Clears the fuse-fault flag after the cause has been fixed. Allowed even with an alarm active.",
"bm_op_write_barcode": "Write the serial number",
"bm_opd_write_barcode": "Writes the serial number (barcode) into the battery. The serial number tells the chip, so a wrong one can lead to a wrong firmware later. Cannot be undone.",
"bm_op_eeprom_erase": "Erase the external memory",
"bm_opd_eeprom_erase": "Erases the battery's EEPROM and restarts it; by default the serial number is written back. Learned data, settings and the barcode are lost. Never cut halfway.",
"bm_op_firmware_update": "Update the firmware",
"bm_opd_firmware_update": "Sends a firmware image to the battery by the maker's bootloader (XMODEM-1K) and writes the serial number back. The wrong image, or a cut during the transfer, can leave the battery dead and void the warranty. The node checks model, chip and image before it sends anything.",
"bm_op_expert_command": "Expert console",
"bm_opd_expert_command": "Sends one console line that no typed operation covers, after the password is asked again and the serial number typed. The answer is shown, recorded and the service password always hidden.",
"hint~nav:overview": "Overview: the state of the perimeter, the cameras and the nodes at a glance.",
